    "item": "type-a-affine-hecke-algebras-and-bernstein-pbw",
    "finding": "The second prose paragraph says it “derives the $A$-basis $\\{X^\\lambda T_w\\}$”. Its theorem thm-hh-affine-type-a-bernstein-pbw instead states that this is an R₀-basis, where A=R₀[X₁^{±1},…,X_n^{±1}]. The displayed family is A-linearly dependent: its elements 1 and X₁ satisfy X₁·1−1·X₁=0. The theorem and its proof correctly give the A-basis (T_w); the page summary mislabels the coefficient ring.",
